't even  fight Melania or Moog during that  playthrough 150 hours later and several  New Game Plus runs under my belt I still  hadn't had enough of Eldon ring I  decided that I was going to try my best  to understand everything about this game  I read every item description started  word docs and Excel spreadsheets to help  connect everything in terms of lore  would I say I was successful at  understanding everything no not even a  little bit even now I can't say I fully  understand Elden Ring's lore I don't  even think that's possible which I  recently accepted but for a few months  earlier this year I was beyond  frustrated I had made some lore videos  that were doing really well for  basically a completely new channel but  of course for every Theory there was a  counter theory that I'd read in the  comments or watch a video of that  completely altered my own Theory and  sent me down a confusing rabbit hole  that constantly had me thinking that I  was just an idiot I felt like I wasn't  capable of understanding eldenring I  kept feeling like a failure in what I  tried to do every single day eventually  I decided to take a step back to take a  small break I found that comparing  myself to other amazing Elden ring  creators was making me worse at making  videos myself comparison is the thief of  Joy so I decided to stop doing it all  together I deleted Twitter I unfollowed  everyone on every platform and I stopped  watching Elden Ring videos on YouTube  now I didn't do this because I disliked  what other creators were making I did  this so I could be the best version of  myself I wish I didn't have to do this  and eventually hopefully I won't but for  now this has worked for me and has  helped me create a narrative with  eldenring that I understand and I enjoy  because I believe this is how the game  was designed for each individual player  to have a different experience playing  that they will come out with different  understandings and beliefs in Elden  Ring's lor